                "lastName": "Luo"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "A Generalized Loss Formula (GLF) is developed for the system losses around an operating point. It is a quasi-osculatory approximation of the exact losses by having the same first and approximately the same second derivatives at the operating point, with respect to three sets of variables: generator powers P<inf xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">g</inf>, generator voltage magnitudes V<inf xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">g</inf>, and transformer tap settings t. The numerical results obtained from two test systems demonstrate that the error in the losses given by the GLF, in comparison to the exact losses from a load flow calculation, is relatively small.",
